Subject: TECH: Would `dark fiber' be vulnerable to jamming?

In regard to white light jamming of the 'dark fiber':

Telephone companies and other owners of lots of cable have to deal
with occasional contruction work that severs a cable by mistake.
A large fiber network would quickly evolve shutoffs to block
signals from a cut fiber, since these often get exposed to 
outside light.  Also, the wavelengths used for fiber are in the
infra-red, so a heat lamp would work better for jamming than a
flashlight.

